# Test: a live edit of service { as112 } reaches the as112 plugin
# Initial config: as112 is disabled with address-family ipv4-only.
# After SIGHUP:   address-family is ipv6-only, nothing else changes.
# Expected: as112 installs the reloaded config at apply and logs it with the
#           new address family.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 22, AC-1: as112's
#            verify/apply pair runs the configure path for the reloaded
#            config (as112Installer.install).
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while as112 kept the boot config until a restart.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the "ipv6-only" line is written only by install, which only
# the apply handler calls on a reload. Without the handler the expectation
# fails. That an edit elsewhere under service publishes nothing is proven in
# Go by TestConfigTxUnchangedSubtreeIsNoop (as112/config_tx_unchanged_test.go).

option=env:var=ze.log.as112:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	as112 {
		enabled false
		address-family ipv4-only
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	as112 {
		enabled false
		address-family ipv6-only
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete:then=stop
expect=stderr:pattern=as112: config applied.*address-family=ipv4-only
expect=stderr:pattern=as112: config applied.*address-family=ipv6-only
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
